findings.body:
`crates/tauri-cli/metadata-v2.json` still reports `tauri` as 2.8.2, but this PR bumps the `tauri` crate to 2.8.3 and commits generated schemas whose `$id` is `https://schema.tauri.app/config/2.8.3`.

::diff{file="crates/tauri-cli/metadata-v2.json" lines="1-6"}

The schema id is derived, not authored: ::file{file="crates/tauri-schema-generator/build.rs"} reads the `tauri` field from this metadata file and writes `https://schema.tauri.app/config/{tauri}` into both ::file{file="crates/tauri-cli/config.schema.json"} and ::file{file="crates/tauri-schema-generator/schemas/config.schema.json"}. Because both schema files changed in this PR, the `check generated files` workflow runs, regenerates them with 2.8.2, and `has-diff.sh` fails on the mismatch. The committed schema cannot be reproduced from this PR's own metadata.

::callout{type="warning"}
The stale metadata also changes what the CLI scaffolds: `tauri init` and `tauri plugin init` emit `tauri = { version = "2.8.2" }` from this field (`crates/tauri-cli/src/init.rs:220`, `crates/tauri-cli/src/plugin/init.rs:118`), so new projects won't reference the just-released 2.8.3.

Fix:

::suggestion{file="crates/tauri-cli/metadata-v2.json" lines="6-6"}
  "tauri": "2.8.3",

`crates/tauri-cli/CHANGELOG.md` announces `Upgraded to tauri-bundler@2.6.1`, and covector's version step did bump the requirement, but the head manifest is back at 2.6.0.

::diff{file="crates/tauri-cli/CHANGELOG.md" lines="3-7"}

The manifest line this release should have changed:

::code{file="crates/tauri-cli/Cargo.toml" lines="50-50"}

`2.6.0` is a caret requirement, so workspace builds still use the local path dependency at 2.6.1 and nothing fails locally. The problem is the published artifact: `tauri-cli@2.8.1` will advertise `tauri-bundler ^2.6.0` on crates.io, so a consumer whose lock already resolves 2.6.0 can keep it and miss the 32-bit Windows binary-patching fix this release exists to ship. It also makes the changelog claim inaccurate and leaves the dependency bump declared in `.changes/config.json` only half-applied.

::suggestion{file="crates/tauri-cli/Cargo.toml" lines="50-50"}
tauri-bundler = { version = "2.6.1", default-features = false, path = "../tauri-bundler" }

The release automation only bumps versions and changelogs; it does not rewrite package metadata. This `homepage` field is a manual addition in a PR whose description is purely generated version updates.

::diff{file="crates/tauri-bundler/Cargo.toml" lines="9-15"}

It is harmless to the crate itself, but unrelated changes in a generated-release PR make it harder to distinguish automation output from hand edits and ship crate metadata changes with no changelog note. Drop it from this branch or land it in a dedicated PR.
